    "title": "Everything You Need to Know About Applying to McNeese State University",
    "text": "McNeese State University has an acceptance rate of 78%. Half the applicants admitted to McNeese State University who submitted test scores have an SAT score between 940 and 1198 or an ACT score of 18 and 23. However, one quarter of admitted applicants achieved scores above these ranges and one quarter scored below these ranges. The application deadline at McNeese State University is Aug. 14. To see additional academic factors along with other school data, learn more about College Compass. McNeese State University Admissions Statsapplication deadlineAug. 14Will You Get Into McNeese State University?College Admissions CalculatorSee How You CompareSign up for a free U.S. News account to see how you stack up against applicants seeking admission at any school.Already have an account?Log in now.InterestedInterestedAppliedAppliedAcceptedAcceptedEnrolledEnrolledRejectedRejectedWaitlistedWaitlistedSee How You CompareSign up for a free U.S. News account to see how you stack up against applicants seeking admission at any school.Already have an account?Log in now.InterestedInterestedAppliedAppliedAcceptedAcceptedEnrolledEnrolledRejectedRejectedWaitlistedWaitlistedData provided by U.S. News College Compass Users.McNeese State University Admissions RequirementsRequired Standardized TestsN/ASAT/ACT Scores Must Be Received ByAug. 12McNeese State University ApplicationsApplication DeadlineAug. 14Early Decision DeadlineN/ACommon Application AcceptedN/ADeadline for housing depositN/APriority application deadlineEntering Class StatsEarly Decision Acceptance RateN/AEarly action acceptance rateAcceptance rate (excluding early action and early decision students)Transfer StudentsAccepting applicationsFall, Spring, SummerMinimum credits to apply18Minimum required college GPA2Guaranteed admission agreement URLN/AInternational StudentsSeparate Application Form RequiredYesConditional admission offeredN/AEarly decision or early action options availableN/ATOEFL (internet-based)Requi